<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>Emailit.Client</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Emailit.Client</AssemblyName>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- NuGet Package Properties -->
    <PackageId>Emailit.Client.v2</PackageId>
    <Version>2.1.0</Version>
    <Authors>Konstanty Chodkowski</Authors>
    <Company>Konstanty Chodkowski Foundation</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 MassMailer</Copyright>
    <Description>A comprehensive .NET client library for the Emailit API v2. Supports all API endpoints including emails, domains, audiences, subscribers, templates, suppressions, email verification, contacts, events, and webhooks. Built on Flurl HTTP with full async/await support, dependency injection integration, and typed exception handling.</Description>
    <PackageTags>emailit;email;api;client;smtp;transactional;email-verification;email-api;webhooks;contacts</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/ChodkowskiFoundation/Emailit.Client.v2</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/ChodkowskiFoundation/Emailit.Client.v2</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v2.1.0 — Email sub-resources, webhook signatures, status rework

New endpoints:
- GetEmailMetaAsync — GET /emails/{id}/meta (metadata without body)
- GetEmailBodyAsync — GET /emails/{id}/body (parsed text/HTML only)
- GetEmailRawAsync — GET /emails/{id}/raw (full MIME message)
- GetEmailAttachmentsAsync — GET /emails/{id}/attachments (base64 content)

New features:
- WebhookSignatureValidator — HMAC-SHA256 webhook signature verification with timing-safe comparison and replay attack protection
- EmailStatus constants — all 12 email statuses after the API status rework (accepted, scheduled, delivered, bounced, attempted, failed, rejected, loaded, clicked, suppressed, received, complained)
- EmailType constants — inbound/outbound email type support

Updated models:
- EmailResponse: added Type field (inbound/outbound)
- ListEmailsRequest: added Type filter
- TemplateResponse: added TotalVersions field
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Flurl" Version="4.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Flurl.Http" Version="4.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>


</Project>
